        "instructions": [
          {
            "id": 238142,
            "primary_message": "In a medium saucepan, bring broth to a boil. Reduce heat to low and gradually add polenta in a thin steady stream, while whisking, until the polenta is incorporated into the broth. Cover and cook, stirring occasionally, until polenta is soft and the texture is creamy, 15-25 minutes.",
            "secondary_message": "48 fl oz (6 cups) chicken or vegetable broth\n1 ½ cups polenta (cornmeal)"
          },
          {
            "id": 238143,
            "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce.",
            "secondary_message": "1 lime\n1 jalapeño pepper\n1 orange bell pepper\n1 pint grape tomatoes\n1 bunch radish\n1 small bunch cilantro\n1 avocado"
          },
          {
            "id": 238144,
            "primary_message": "Juice lime into a medium bowl. Add oil, salt, and pepper; whisk to combine the dressing.",
            "secondary_message": "4 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
          },
          {
            "id": 238145,
            "primary_message": "Peel and mince garlic. Peel, halve, and thinly slice shallots into half-moons; add both to the bowl with the dressing.",
            "secondary_message": "2 cloves garlic\n2 shallots"
          },
          {
            "id": 238146,
            "primary_message": "Halve jalapeño pepper lengthwise; seed and remove ribs with a spoon. Slice crosswise into thin half-moons; add to the bowl. (Be careful, with jalapeños, do not touch your eyes and ensure you wash your hands after handling or wear gloves while preparing.)",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 238147,
            "primary_message": "Trim, seed, and medium dice bell pepper; add to the bowl.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 238148,
            "primary_message": "Halve tomatoes and add to the bowl. Trim, halve, and slice radishes into thin half-moons. Add both to the bowl.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 238149,
            "primary_message": "Shave cilantro leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Add to the bowl and stir to combine the salad; set aside.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 238150,
            "primary_message": "Preheat a skillet over medium heat.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 238151,
            "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, drain and rinse beans in a colander.",
            "secondary_message": "2 (15 oz) cans pinto beans"
          },
          {
            "id": 238152,
            "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add beans and spices to the skillet; cook, stirring occasionally, until beans are warmed through, 2-3 minutes. Cover and remove from heat.",
            "secondary_message": "2 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n½ tsp cumin, ground\n½ tsp paprika\n¼ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
          },
          {
            "id": 238153,
            "primary_message": "While the beans are cooking, coarsely grate the cheese.",
            "secondary_message": "½ (8 oz) block cheddar cheese"
          },
          {
            "id": 238154,
            "primary_message": "Add cheese, salt, and pepper to the polenta and stir to combine; if the polenta is too firm, add hot water, 1 tablespoon at a time, until you reach a desired consistency. Cover and remove from heat.",
            "secondary_message": "½ tsp salt\n½ tsp black pepper"
          },
          {
            "id": 238155,
            "primary_message": "Halve and pit the avocado. Slice thinly while still in skin, then scoop out with a spoon.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 238156,
            "primary_message": "To serve, divide polenta, beans, and salad between bowls. Top with avocado and enjoy!",
            "secondary_message": null
          }
        ],
